// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/petal_pulse_viz.t27 -- petal N (PULSE, petal index 13) of the interactive visualization
; epic. Refs epic t27#12173 (issue t27#12334). Built on specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27; it agrees
; with row N of specs/t27f/petal_viz_plan.t27 (reps 1792 = timeline + chart + badge, truth VERIFIED).
; --
; Question: "Which of the 27 domains is moving, which is quiet, which is blocked?" Six sample domains
; over five ticks are shown as a timeline (a row per domain, a cell per tick, each the domain's class
; at that tick), a chart (how many domains are active, warm, quiet and blocked at the tick) and a
; badge (the same counts, how many are moving, and the truth label). The reader steps the tick, may
; add one recorded commit to one domain (the choice), and selects a domain or a cell and sees it lit
; in the rows, the cells and the chart.
; --
; Source of truth: specs/t27os/domain_pulse.t27 owns the rules; this petal calls its pub fns and
; never copies them: the lamp rule status_of (BLOCKED wins, never committed is QUIET, under a day
; ACTIVE, under a week WARM, else QUIET), status_text, the age bucket bucket_of, the log parsers
; rec_next and rec_time, and the constants ST_QUIET, ST_WARM, ST_ACTIVE, ST_BLOCKED, DAY, WEEK, BUCKETS.
; --
; Recorded petal-side data (disclosed here and in the report). The source's readers of a whole log,
; of the red list and of its domain names and letters reach per-domain tables of other specs that
; t27c gen cannot splice into another module (it prints them as unresolved), so this petal cannot
; call them and records three things itself: (1) six sample domains, the menu petals A, D, J, N, U
; and Ti (petal_letter_byte), a sample of the 27; (2) one commit log per domain in the source's own
; record format (a 0x1e byte, a hash, a 0x1f byte, the unix time, a 0x1f byte, a subject, a blank
; line, a path), read by the source's rec_next and rec_time; (3) the ticks at which a domain's lamp
; is red, since the source keeps no red list to read. The RULES applied to that data are the
; source's, the data is not. The clock is petal-side too: tick t is T0 plus two days per tick.
; --
; Layers:
;   L1 state     one VizState, every input through viz_apply: step = the tick (0..4), param = the
;                choice (0 the recorded data, c in 1..6 one added commit in domain c - 1).
;   L2 entities  domain d = viz_ref(NODE, d); cell (d, t) = viz_ref(CELL, d * 8 + t); focus 0..5.
;   L3 rules     pnv_last, pnv_status_at, pnv_bucket_at, pnv_count: the logs asked of the source.
;   L4 truth     VERIFIED while every value is the source's rule over the recorded logs; an added
;                commit is a what-if, so the badge drops to DEMO (viz_may_claim).
;   L5 views     timeline, chart and badge, each a plain function of the one VizState.
;   L6 host      pnv_host: badge, timeline and chart as three root slots, in frame coordinates.
; --
; Integer only. Not claimed: no host draws this petal yet (wiring it into specs/t27os/
; glass_window.t27 is a child issue of the epic), and the logs are a recorded sample, not the live
; git history of the 27 domains.

